      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:cyclotron",
      "title": "Cyclotron",
      "text": "Protons spiralling outward between two copper dees, kicked across the gap twice a turn by a radio-frequency voltage that must keep exact step with them.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the field, then tune the RF to the protons' cyclotron frequency, f = qB/2\u03c0m (15.25 MHz per tesla). The beam reaches E = (qBR)\u00b2/2m at the extraction radius; as it gains energy its mass grows and it slips out of phase - keep the slip under 90\u00b0. Above 2.2 T the iron saturates. Beam power heats the target."
    },
